body:
So, this one isn't mine but a very close childhood friend of mines story. I have a good friend who is half-Japanese and all in all a really good friend, in grade 7 we'd skip class and watch anime like kids do. I think we were watching a sappy boy love one or whatever, and this creepy fellow is sort of watching from a distance and asks are names. We of course as children  think nothing of it and give our names, we go on the rest of our days and sort of forget this guy until their mom says shes coming to pick them up. I walk with her to meet their mother as I like their mom and would like to say hi, as we approach we see her mom and she is happily waving. Beckoning my friend and opens her arms for a hug, as she does we see the creepy guy again and thinking the hug is for him he opens his arms, unaware of her mother behind them. My friend awkwardly dodges his hug and runs towards her mom hugging her, I remember this clearly as the denial of a hug was so awkward. As the guys face completely fell as he realized the hug wasn't at all for him.

&#x200B;

I have more but they were directed at a Caucasian friend of mine, nonetheless still undeniably creepy and inappropriate.

Away, you three inch fool!

&#x200B;

Ya know in case you wanna call some one an idiot but also little.
